ot columns is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-130959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c680fda06fa2f83e46075e6ebe9b567cd34ab2f0257707276276bc6230ca565"} {"question" "q-130959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-130959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-130959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0 & 20 & -35 & 24\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 0 & 20 & -35 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c680fda06fa2f83e46075e6ebe9b567cd34ab2f0257707276276bc6230ca565"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-35452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-73639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-73639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 0 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $2$nd, $3$rd, $5$th and $6$th columns." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "188a90c8d285115c8f9782c0822a031f73e5b982e9d16da506e3298b12c81776"} {"question" "q-73639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "categor