tion" "e-4704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/example-4704.json" "file_sha256" "b73b0d77801282c1979bd221e32df37aa1ea54dd4f324aeabe50f0ae38959dc1"} {"question" "e-4704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/example-4704.json" "file_sha256" "b73b0d77801282c1979bd221e32df37aa1ea54dd4f324aeabe50f0ae38959dc1"} {"question" "e-4705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/example-4705.json" "file_sha256" "c2781f4d5cb3175e8cd7d9ba772b78d3609cb1212382f76568e0c75505774f53"} {"question" "e-4705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 