 [17592186124207 :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124207 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3}:=R_{3} + 2R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3$."] [17592186124208 :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B$, given by\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186124208 :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{3} &:=R_{3} + 2R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & R_{4}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{4} + (-\\frac{2}{7})R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $B$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186121937 17592186121938 17592186121939 17592186121940 17592186121941 17592186121949 17592186121950 17592186121951 17592186121952 17592186121953 17592186121955 17592186121956 17592186121957 17592186121958 17592186121959 17592186121973 17592186121974 17592186121975 17592186121976 17592186121977] "immutable_fields" [[17592186121936 :answer-field/correct] [17592186121936 :answer-field/id] [17592186121936 :answer-